Well, the English is a bit murky, but the Lojban (after the equation of 
{zo'e} with {su'o da}, which does not look right at all) is clear.  The first 
is true if each language has an inventor, even if it is a different one each 
time.  The second is true if there is one person (or group of people, 
perhaps) who invented (together, if a group) every single language.
           
